A provider that is not on any registry is a terraform_provider whose files is the built binary, used like a hub-provided one: go_binary( name = "terraform-provider-custom", # the engine requires this prefix srcs = ["main.go"],
) terraform_provider( name = "custom", files = [":terraform-provider-custom"], source = "example/custom", # matches `required_providers` version = "1.0.0",
) terraform_module( name = "app", srcs = glob(["*.tf"]), lock = ".terraform.lock.hcl", deps = [":custom"],
) Leave platform unset: it is read from the configuration the provider is built in. The lock still needs an entry for the provider, written by hand with the version and a placeholder h1:; the build replaces the hash with that of the binary it installed. A module that depends on providers but has no lock is an analysis error.

