A root module new to Bazel is a directory of .tf files. Three things get added around it: BUILD targets, a provider lock, and a deps tag in MODULE.bazel that fetches what the lock and the module blocks name. Gazelle writes the BUILD targets. Set up Gazelle with the rules' language and run it: # BUILD.bazel at the repository root
load("@gazelle//:def.bzl", "gazelle", "gazelle_binary") gazelle_binary( name = "gazelle_bin", languages = ["@rules_terraform//terraform/gazelle"],
) gazelle( name = "gazelle", gazelle = ":gazelle_bin",
) bazel run //:gazelle writes a terraform_module per directory of configuration, deps between them following the local module blocks, and for a root (a directory with a backend or cloud block, or a # gazelle:tf_kind root directive) a terraform_binary named terraform and a terraform_providers_lock named providers_lock.update. Generate the lock and commit it. This runs the toolchain engine's providers lock for every platform in the default set and writes .terraform.lock.hcl next to the sources; it needs the network. bazel run //path/to/app:providers_lock.update Rerun it whenever a required_providers block changes. Declare the deps tag in MODULE.bazel. Gazelle names the hub a root depends on @tf_<path> with / and - replaced by _, or whatever a # gazelle:tf_deps_hub directive says; the tag must use that name. terraform = use_extension("@rules_terraform//terraform:extensions.bzl", "terraform")
terraform.deps( name = "tf_path_to_app", lock = "//path/to/app:.terraform.lock.hcl", roots = ["//path/to/app:main.tf"], # only if its `module` blocks name registry or git modules
)
use_repo(terraform, "tf_path_to_app") Run Gazelle again. With the lock in place it adds the terraform_providers_lock_test, which fails when the lock drifts from the sources. Then: bazel test //path/to/app/... # validate, fmt, lock drift
bazel run //path/to/app:terraform -- plan # the engine, offline for providers and modules Without Gazelle the same targets are written by hand; the monorepo example shows them for three environments sharing one lock. Add .terraform/ to .gitignore: the rules read nothing from it, and init writes it.

